      "question_text": "Triple test in 2nd trimester for Down syndrome shows?",
      "options": {
        "A": "↑AFP, ↑hCG, ↑estriol",
        "B": "↓AFP, ↑hCG, ↓estriol",
        "C": "↑AFP, ↓hCG, ↑estriol",
        "D": "↓AFP, ↓hCG, ↓estriol"
      },
      "correct_answer": "B",
      "explanation": "Down syndrome (T21) triple test: ↓AFP, ↑hCG, ↓unconjugated estriol (uE3). Quadruple test adds inhibin A (↑). Neural tube defects: ↑AFP."
