      "question_text": "Magnesium sulfate in eclampsia: first sign of toxicity?",
      "options": {
        "A": "Respiratory depression",
        "B": "Loss of patellar reflexes",
        "C": "Cardiac arrest",
        "D": "Muscle weakness"
      },
      "correct_answer": "B",
      "explanation": "MgSO4 toxicity sequence: loss of DTRs (8-10 mg/dL) → respiratory paralysis (12-15) → cardiac arrest (>15). Monitor: RR >12/min, UO >25 mL/hr, patellar reflexes present. Antidote: calcium gluconate."
